P0:
- export sheet emitted sales/production as the price; now reads the price lever (#72)
- input sheet covered 7 of 19 forms; H6 contract delivery, H1-2, H2, A4 and the rest
  are now emitted in real entry order, with unplanned-but-required forms listed (#73)
- an area could hold only one product per quarter, so 48,000 chips + 18,000 PCs in
  Europe was inexpressible; rl.lines[] plus linesOf() normalises every consumer (#74)
- contract config contradicted the signed agreement: clause 5 fallback, price, currency,
  collection schedule and the 15% penalty are now modelled (#40)
- no price = no sale is a hard export block, not a checklist tick (#46)
- the AI plan validator never checked chip coverage (#4)

P1:
- breach tested consolidated cash only; regional deficits now break the floor (#22)
- deficits carry the Data Log 07 negative-balance rate (#24)
- quarterly interest was divided by 4 (#25)
- R&D was split /4 in cash and /3 in P&L; booked once at HQ (#27)
- chip stock counted globally, ignoring region (#1); contract chips double-counted (#2)
- MR3/MR74 free/paid inverted vs the booklet; full catalog with costs added (#64, #65)
- selling cost per unit and depreciation were dead constants (#30, #31)
- R&D granted grades deterministically on an invented threshold; now a calibrated
  probability with an explicit confidence label (#14-16)
- assortment was listed as a demand determinant and modelled nowhere (#47)

Tests: tests/audit-fixes.cjs (26 assertions), tests/boot-smoke.cjs (real jsdom boot).
